================================================================================
GAME DATA
================================================================================

Asset licensing policy, approved sources, and the intake checklist are documented
in docs/ASSETS.md. That document is authoritative; this file records only what is
actually shipped.

OpenFPS ships only game data licensed CC0 1.0, MIT, or BSD 2/3-clause. See
docs/ASSETS.md section 3 for the full policy and the rationale for excluding
CC-BY, CC-BY-SA, and copyleft-licensed assets.

CC0 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/) is a public-domain
dedication and imposes no attribution requirement. Contributors whose work is
listed below are credited voluntarily, as a courtesy rather than an obligation.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOURCE DISTRIBUTION: no game data.

Assets are not part of the source tree — assets/models is gitignored — and a
clone of this repository contains no third-party art of any kind. They are
produced locally by `gradlew :tools:regenerateDemoAssets` from packs downloaded
by hand; see docs/DEMO_ASSETS.md.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ANDROID APK: Kenney models, CC0 1.0.

This is the one build that ships game data, because it must — an app cannot read
the developer's filesystem, so the models are packaged into the APK's assets/ by
the `stageModelAssets` task. An APK built from a fresh clone therefore contains
no art at all and comes up as a menu; an APK built after staging the packs
contains the following.

    Kenney Prototype Kit
        Author:      Kenney (Kenney Vleugels / kenney.nl)
        Source:      https://kenney.nl/assets/prototype-kit
        License:     CC0 1.0 Universal
        License URL: http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
        Shipped as:  assets/models/level/*.ofm — floor-square, wall,
                     wall-doorway, wall-corner, column, crate, stairs,
                     shape-slope. Converted from the pack's GLB models to this
                     project's .ofm format by :tools; the geometry and textures
                     are Kenney's, the container is ours.

    Kenney Blaster Kit
        Author:      Kenney (Kenney Vleugels / kenney.nl)
        Source:      https://kenney.nl/assets/blaster-kit
        License:     CC0 1.0 Universal
        License URL: http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
        Shipped as:  assets/models/weapon/blaster-b.ofm — the first-person
                     viewmodel.

    Kenney Blocky Characters
        Author:      Kenney (Kenney Vleugels / kenney.nl)
        Source:      https://kenney.nl/assets/blocky-characters
        License:     CC0 1.0 Universal
        License URL: http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
        Shipped as:  assets/models/character/character-*.ofm — the opponents.

CC0 imposes no attribution requirement, and Kenney's own readme says so in as
many words: "Support by crediting 'Kenney' or 'www.kenney.nl' (this is not a
requirement)". The credit above is therefore voluntary. It is given anyway,
prominently and by pack, because this project would have no art at all without
it — and because a reader of an APK's asset list deserves to know whose work
they are looking at without having to go and find out.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AUDIO: no third-party sound, in any build.

Every sound OpenFPS makes is generated at runtime by this project's own
`com.openfps.engine.audio.synth.BlasterSound` — a pitch sweep and an amplitude
envelope, computed into 16-bit PCM in about forty lines of arithmetic and wrapped
in a RIFF/WAVE header by `WavAudio`. It is covered by this repository's MIT
license, like any other source file here.

There is no sound file in this repository, none in the APK, none downloaded by
`fetchAssets`, and no audio decoder beyond what libGDX already carries for other
purposes. That is a deliberate answer to an open question rather than an
oversight: docs/ASSETS.md section 3's accepted-sources table covers models and
textures and has no audio row, so shipping a .wav would have forced the source,
format and container questions all at once — for one blaster noise. Generating it
settles all three by removing them.

If a real sound bank is ever added, it enters through the section 7 intake
checklist like anything else and is recorded above, by pack, with author, source,
license and license URL. Until then this line is the whole of the audio
provenance, and it is complete.

The playback path uses OpenAL Soft (desktop, via LWJGL — recorded above under
DESKTOP LAUNCHER ONLY) and the Android platform's own audio services. Neither
contributes content.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated greybox room (assets/models/generated-room.ofm) is produced by
this project's own `com.openfps.tools.model.ProceduralRoom` and is covered by
this repository's MIT license. It is the fallback for a clone with no Kenney
packs staged, and it is deliberately reported at WARN so nobody mistakes it for
Kenney art. See DemoModels.

Each asset entering the tree is recorded here with its source, author, license,
and license URL, per the intake checklist in docs/ASSETS.md section 7.
